text.section:
An inspection of any facility may include an assessment of the following:

Any policies and procedures related to the care of inmates;


Conditions of confinement;


Availability of educational and rehabilitative programming, drug and mental health treatment, and inmate jobs and vocational training;


Any policies and procedures related to visitation;


Any medical facilities and medical policies and procedures;


Any lockdowns at the facility in the time since the last inspection or, in the instance of the initial inspection, any lockdowns at the facility within the previous three years;


Staffing at the facility, including the number of staff, job assignments, the ratio of staff to inmates, and the number of staff vacancies;


Physical or sexual assaults at the facility in the time since the last inspection or, in the instance of the initial inspection, any physical or sexual assaults within the previous three years;


Inmate or staff deaths at the facility in the time since the last inspection or, in the instance of the initial inspection, any inmate or staff deaths within the previous three years;


Any policies and procedures related to Department staff recruitment, training, supervision, and discipline;


Availability of complaint and grievance forms at the facility and the accessibility of the administrative remedies process to inmates and their representatives; and


Any other aspect of the operation of the facility that the Office determines is necessary to assess or that relates to covered issues.
